+              Offer a mix of climbing spots, scratching posts, puzzle feeders,
+              and interactive toys. Rotating toys and scheduling short play
+              sessions each day helps prevent boredom.
+            </p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="example">
+          <button
+            class="question"
+            type="button"
+            aria-expanded="false"
+            aria-controls="answer-5"
+            id="question-5"
+          >
+            Why do cats flick their tails?
+            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+          </button>
+          <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" hidden>
+            <p>
+              Tail movement is a clue to mood. A gentle upright tail can show
+              confidence and friendliness, while quick flicking may mean your
+              cat is alert, overstimulated, or annoyed.
+            </p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
